add('comment-yeung','Left column quotation attributed to Edward S. Yeung','expert_comment','Iowa State chemist Edward S. Yeung discusses nanocrystal tags as a class of stains that may complement or replace techniques for cell imaging, DNA sequencing, immunoassay and other analyses. This is an attributed outlook, not demonstrated performance across all applications.')
add('comment-mirkin-advantages','Left-column ending continued below central schematic','expert_comment','Northwestern chemist Chad A. Mirkin highlights tunable emission spectra and possible advantages over typical organic dyes. No numerical tuning range or performance comparison is supplied.')
add('comment-mirkin-yield','Middle column below schematic','expert_comment','Mirkin cautions that particle quantum yields could limit assay sensitivity. No quantum-yield value or sensitivity measurement is reported.')
add('context-nie-spectra','Middle column discussion attributed to Shuming Nie','secondary_optical_context','Nie describes quantum-dot fluorescence as narrower and brighter than rhodamine 6G or other organic dyes. No FWHM, absolute intensity, quantum yield, excitation condition or controlled comparison is reproduced.')
