add('context-photostability','Middle column illumination comparison','secondary_optical_context','The article states that semiconductor particles can continue emitting, in some cases, 100 times longer than dye molecules under prolonged illumination. Preserve the qualification and comparative nature; no absolute duration, dose, irradiance, named sample or test protocol is provided.')
add('surface-indiana-maa','Middle-column bottom, continued at top of right column','secondary_surface_context','Shuming Nie and graduate student Warren C. W. Chan react ZnS-capped CdSe with mercaptoacetic acid. The report links this treatment to water solubility and binding to proteins, peptides and other biomolecules. Amounts, solvent, pH, temperature, duration, workup and activation/coupling reagents are absent.')
add('bio-transferrin','Right column upper biological example','secondary_biological_context','Human-cell receptors reportedly recognize quantum-dot-tagged transferrin and allow entry into the cells. No cell-line identity, assay conditions, quantitative uptake or synthesis-to-assay specimen join is supplied.')
add('bio-immunorecognition','Right column upper biological example','secondary_biological_context','The Indiana team reportedly demonstrates that labeled immunomolecules recognize specific antibodies or antigens. No species list, binding constant, assay recipe or experimental dataset is supplied.')
