add('optical-size-colors','Right column size/emission comparison','secondary_optical_context','The news text describes dots with 2 nm cores as green-emitting and 4 nm sized particles as red-emitting. The wording does not define the same core/overall-diameter basis for both. No wavelengths, size distributions or primary sizing method are supplied.')
add('bio-two-color-staining','Right column paragraph following size/emission comparison','secondary_biological_context','Differentially functionalized larger and smaller particles selectively color mouse-cell nuclei green and another cell portion red in a simultaneous two-color example. The supplied caption identifies the red features as cell filaments; no protocol quantities or acquisition settings are provided.')
add('outlook-ten-color','Right column two-color paragraph ending','author_outlook','A ten-color experiment is presented as a prospective claim, not a demonstrated ten-color image or ten sets of synthesized particles.')
add('outlook-basic-research','Right column closing quotation','expert_comment','Alivisatos reflects on roughly 15 years of quantum-dot/basic nanocrystal research and unexpected molecular-biology applications alongside possible optoelectronic applications. This is historical perspective, not an experiment or quantitative materials property.')
